const body = `<h1>8.4a — DungeonMap: The 2D Grid Foundation</h1>

<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">RPG Build</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>Your DungeonCrawl game has been room-by-room so far. But real dungeons are
    grids — rooms connected by corridors, with walls, treasure, and monsters at
    specific coordinates. Today you create the grid itself: a 2D char array with
    wall borders and the ability to set and read individual tiles.</p>

    <p>Open the <a href="../docs/unit-08/dungeon-map.html">Dungeon Map
    Builder (Student RPG Guide)</a>. Follow Part 1.</p>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Build: DungeonMap.java — The Grid</h3>
        <p>Create <code>DungeonMap.java</code>:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Private field: <code>char[][] tiles</code></li>
            <li>Constructor takes rows and cols, fills entire grid with '.' (floor)</li>
            <li>Place wall borders: top row, bottom row, left col, right col all '#'</li>
            <li><code>setTile(int row, int col, char symbol)</code> — sets a single tile</li>
            <li><code>getTile(int row, int col)</code> — returns tile or ' ' if out of bounds</li>
            <li><code>display()</code> — prints the entire grid with a space after each char</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>You fill the grid with '.' then overwrite edges with '#'. Why two
                passes? Could you do it in one nested loop?</li>
            <li>getTile() returns ' ' for out-of-bounds instead of crashing.
                Why is this safer? Where in your future code will this matter?</li>
            <li>display() uses <code>tiles.length</code> for rows and
                <code>tiles[0].length</code> for columns. What happens if the
                grid has 0 rows?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Acceptance — your DungeonMap must:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Display a bordered rectangle of floor tiles</li>
            <li>Allow setting and reading individual tiles</li>
            <li>Handle out-of-bounds reads without crashing</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-08/dungeon-map.html">Dungeon Map Builder (Student RPG Guide)</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-08/2d-array-basics.html">2D Array Basics</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
